WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.067
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.801
Welcome, welcome,
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:05.901
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:07.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.300
Guys, it is the holiday season,

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.868
and today, it even started
snowing here in New York.

00:00:11.868 --> 00:00:13.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:14.834
Yeah, it was just a few flakes,

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:18.267
but LaGuardia
shut down immediately.

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:20.467
Well, here's some fun
local news.

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:21.567
You guys aren't
going to believe this.

00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:23.968
A guy in Brooklyn
just won $10 million

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:27.567
from a scratch-off ticket
for the second year in a row.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.601
Yeah, he's loving life today.

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:33.501
He marched into his old job
like, "I quit again!"

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:39.601
Well, guys, everyone is
talking about this.

00:00:39.601 --> 00:00:42.501
Last night in Alabama,
four candidates took the stage

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:45.367
for another Republican
presidential debate.

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:47.167
Yep. The big winners from
the night were

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:48.601
Nikki Haley, Chris Christie,

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:52.334
and everyone who decided
not to watch.

00:00:52.334 --> 00:00:55.300
Yeah, last night was
the fourth Republican debate.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.701
At this point, it's kind of
like "Indiana Jones" movies.

00:00:57.701 --> 00:00:59.434
Three was enough.
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:02.367
Once again, the debate
was kind of crazy.

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:04.334
People are saying it was
pretty controversial

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:06.467
when Vivek Ramaswamy
held up a sign

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:08.434
that said "Nikki=corrupt."

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:09.567
-Ooh!

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:12.334
-I don't think that that's
controversial.

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:13.734
I mean, I think it would be
really controversial

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:14.934
if he held up a sign
that said...

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:18.267
I mean, because that's --
People are --

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:21.167
That is not --
A hot dog is a hot dog.

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:22.901
Meanwhile, Chris Christie
came out swinging

00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:25.200
and went after Ramaswamy
and he really didn't hold back.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.501
Watch this. For real.

00:01:26.501 --> 00:01:28.434
-You do this at every debate.
-I'll say exactly --

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:31.267
-No, don't interrupt me.
I didn't interrupt you.

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:33.634
This is the fourth debate,
the fourth debate

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:36.400
that you would be voted,
in the first 20 minutes,

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.901
as the most obnoxious
blowhard in America.

00:01:38.901 --> 00:01:42.334
So shut up for a --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:45.501
-Wow. Wow!

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:47.501
It is clear Ramaswamy
isn't well-liked.

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:48.701
After he attacked Christie,

00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:50.334
the moderators were like,
"Governor Christie,

00:01:50.334 --> 00:01:53.100
you have two hours to respond."

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.868
At another point
during the debate,

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:56.601
Chris Christie said
the other candidates

00:01:56.601 --> 00:01:59.934
were afraid to mention Trump
and treat him like Voldemort,

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:01.767
he who must not be named.

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:02.834
And that got me thinking.

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:04.067
There's actually
a lot of similarities

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:05.601
between Republicans
and Harry Potter.

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:08.501
-Oh, boy. Here we go.

00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:10.133
-What's up, Tariq?
-Well, let me guess.

00:02:10.133 --> 00:02:12.534
You're going to show,
like, a bunch of side-by-side

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:15.367
photos of Republicans
and then the Harry Potter --

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:16.901
like, the characters
that they look like.

00:02:16.901 --> 00:02:18.667
-Yeah, that was the plan.

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:20.067
-Well, I know exactly
how this will go.

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:23.100
So, first, you'll show
a picture of Harry Potter,

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:27.467
and then you'll say he looks
like House Speaker Mike Johnson.

00:02:28.234 --> 00:02:29.868
And then, after that,
you'll show a picture of --

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:32.734
I don't know --
probably Draco Malfoy,

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:36.167
and you'll say he looks
like Eric Trump.

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:39.133
And then, finally, after that,
you'll show a picture of --

00:02:39.133 --> 00:02:41.234
I don't know -- like,
Neville Longbottom

00:02:41.234 --> 00:02:42.901
when he got frozen,
and then, boom,

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:44.567
there he is, Mitch McConnell.

00:02:44.567 --> 00:02:46.767
Is that how this is going to go?

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:49.734
-I mean, yeah, yeah,
that was pretty good,

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:51.968
but you're a little off.

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:54.701
Yeah. Because, first,
I'd show Harry Potter,

00:02:54.701 --> 00:02:57.868
but then I'd say he looks
like George Santos.

00:02:57.868 --> 00:03:00.300
Then, after that,
I'd show Draco's dad,

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:02.634
Lucius Malfoy,
and say he looks like

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:04.767
Marjorie Taylor Greene.

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:08.033
And, finally, I'd show
frozen Neville Longbottom,

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:11.567
but he's more like Ron DeSantis
trying to stand normally.

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:15.868
-I got to give it to you, man.
-Yeah?

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:17.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:17.567 --> 00:03:19.234
That's right, everybody.

00:03:19.234 --> 00:03:21.801
The debate lasted two hours,
and a lot happened,

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.367
so it was honestly hard
to keep up.

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:25.434
Thankfully, we have a remix
to help you out. Check it out.

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:26.634
-Let's get started.
[ Hip-hop music playing ]

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:28.100
-Nikki is corrupt.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.667
-It's not worth my time
to respond.

00:03:29.667 --> 00:03:30.868
-That's not true.

00:03:30.868 --> 00:03:33.067
-Don't interrupt me.
I didn't interrupt you.

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:34.701
-I have a woman problem.

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:36.801
-The most obnoxious
blowhard in America.

00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:39.300
-Walk yourself off that stage,
enjoy a nice meal.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.367
-Don't interrupt me.
I didn't interrupt you.

00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:42.501
-They all had man dresses on.

00:03:42.501 --> 00:03:43.701
-Get the hell out of this race.

00:03:43.701 --> 00:03:45.534
-Don't interrupt me.
I didn't interrupt you.

00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:47.334
-Thanks for watching.
Thank you, guys.

00:03:47.334 --> 00:03:49.467
-There you go.
Just a little remix.

00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:51.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:55.767
-Well, switching gears, guys,
this is very sweet.

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:57.501
Apparently,
every year for Christmas,

00:03:57.501 --> 00:03:59.400
President Biden
gives his wife, Jill,

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.334
a personal poem
that he's written.

00:04:01.334 --> 00:04:03.133
-Aww!
-Isn't that cute?

00:04:03.133 --> 00:04:04.467
Yeah, and this year,
he's been writing a bunch,

00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:06.067
trying to find
the right one to give.

00:04:06.067 --> 00:04:08.234
And we actually got a hold
of the wastebasket

00:04:08.234 --> 00:04:12.234
from the Oval Office
that has some of the rejects.

00:04:12.234 --> 00:04:13.467
Should I read
some of them right now?

00:04:13.467 --> 00:04:15.367
-I would, yeah.
-This is the official waste...

00:04:15.367 --> 00:04:18.234
-Wow!
-...of the Oval Office.

00:04:18.234 --> 00:04:20.033
James, can I get some
poem-reading music, please?

00:04:20.033 --> 00:04:22.133
[ Soft music plays ]

00:04:22.133 --> 00:04:23.801
Oh, that's perfect.

00:04:33.601 --> 00:04:36.601
Sweet, right?

00:04:36.601 --> 00:04:38.901
This one here.
How about this one? Oh!

00:04:38.901 --> 00:04:41.267
-He really crumpled them up.
-This says...

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:51.467
-Aww!
-Isn't that sweet?

00:04:51.467 --> 00:04:53.200
-That's cute.
-It's cute.

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:56.901
He did crumble them up.
He did crumble them all up.

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:58.133
Yeah.
-Really hard.

00:04:58.133 --> 00:04:59.701
-Yeah. Well, he probably
shoots them in the basket.

00:04:59.701 --> 00:05:01.734
-Yeah, probably did that
from a long distance.

00:05:07.934 --> 00:05:12.000
So, I mean, that's...

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.601
-Oh, there's another one.
-Yeah.

00:05:13.601 --> 00:05:16.667
-He wrote a lot of these.
-Yeah. Oh, this is nice.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.734
Well, it's close.

00:05:25.734 --> 00:05:27.234
He's cl--
-He's close.

00:05:27.234 --> 00:05:30.534
-He means well.

00:05:30.534 --> 00:05:34.868
This is the last one here.
-Wow, that one looks glued.

00:05:40.834 --> 00:05:43.968
There you go. That's fantastic.
Isn't that nice?

00:05:43.968 --> 00:05:45.334
That's cute.

00:05:45.334 --> 00:05:48.133
Merry Christmas, everybody.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:48.133 --> 00:05:49.467
We got the wastebasket.
-Wow.

00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:53.834
That's so great you got that.
-Yeah. You guys see this?

00:05:53.834 --> 00:05:56.467
A new poll found that
New York City Mayor Eric Adams'

00:05:56.467 --> 00:05:59.767
approval rating is at 28%,

00:05:59.767 --> 00:06:02.200
which is the lowest
in that poll's history.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:03.434
Yeah, he's pretty unpopular.

00:06:03.434 --> 00:06:05.467
Check out this news thing
I saw, local news.

00:06:05.467 --> 00:06:09.234
-Mayor Eric Adams' approval
rating is now at a record low,

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:10.868
according to a recent poll.

00:06:10.868 --> 00:06:13.901
To put that in perspective,
he's now less popular than...

00:06:34.968 --> 00:06:36.801
and even...

00:06:36.801 --> 00:06:39.434
-Oh, my God!
That was in the local news.

00:06:39.434 --> 00:06:40.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:40.734 --> 00:06:42.167
Hey...

00:06:42.167 --> 00:06:44.667
-Hey!

00:06:44.667 --> 00:06:47.367
-Switching gears, I read that,
on a recent flight from Canada,

00:06:47.367 --> 00:06:49.234
an off-duty pilot had to step in

00:06:49.234 --> 00:06:52.534
after the captain suffered
an uncontrollable nosebleed.

00:06:52.534 --> 00:06:54.701
Yeah. This is why
before I board a plane,

00:06:54.701 --> 00:06:57.634
I always double-check that
the pilot's not a third grader.

00:06:57.634 --> 00:06:59.634
[ Laughter ]

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:04.300
And this made things worse.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:06.234
Instead of tilting his head back
to stop the bleeding,

00:07:06.234 --> 00:07:07.267
he tilted the plane.

00:07:07.267 --> 00:07:08.734
-Oh.
-Yeah, it was...

00:07:08.734 --> 00:07:12.767
Guys, finally, we have
exactly 12 shows left

00:07:12.767 --> 00:07:15.767
before we go on Christmas break,
which means it's time for that

00:07:15.767 --> 00:07:17.434
beloved "Tonight Show"
tradition.

00:07:17.434 --> 00:07:21.868
It's time for
"12 Days of Christmas Sweaters"!

00:07:21.868 --> 00:07:24.267
-♪ "12 Days of
Christmas Sweaters" ♪

00:07:24.267 --> 00:07:29.334
♪ 12 days left ♪

00:07:29.334 --> 00:07:30.467
-That's right.

00:07:30.467 --> 00:07:33.968
Every show between
now and Christmas,

00:07:33.968 --> 00:07:36.801
